                "version_or_split": "1092 single-gene perturbations"
              }
            ],
            "evidence_spans": [
              {
                "content": "AttentionPert achieves near-zero error on perturbations to FOXA transcription factor family.",
                "provenance": {
                  "chunk_id": "b075860377568b9135db",
                  "page_end": 6,
                  "page_start": 6,
                  "paraphrased": false,
                  "text_excerpt": "AttentionPert achieves near-zero error on perturbations to the FOXA transcription factor family across all genes, suggesting that these are degenerate cases where the complexity of the transcriptome decreases in their absence."
                },
                "span_id": "span_3"
              },
              {
                "content": "Code is available at https://github.com/BaiDing1234/AttentionPert.",
                "provenance": {
                  "chunk_id": "c91d3773bbbc4a4849a4",
                  "page_end": 1,
                  "page_start": 1,
                  "paraphrased": false,
                  "text_excerpt": "Code is available at https://github.com/BaiDing1234/AttentionPert."
                },
                "span_id": "span_1"
              },
              {
                "content": "Data available with accession numbers GSE133344 (Norman et al. 2019) and GSE146194 (Replogle et al. 2022).",
                "provenance": {
                  "chunk_id": "f8cd38ce362cc11f852c",
                  "page_end": 8,
                  "page_start": 8,
                  "paraphrased": false,
                  "text_excerpt": "The data underlying this article are available in Gene Expression Omnibus at https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/, and can be accessed with accession numbers GSE133344 (Norman et al. 2019) and GSE146194 (Replogle et al. 2022)."
                },
                "span_id": "span_2"
              }
            ],
            "experiments_or_tasks": [
              "Predict post-perturbation gene expressions given specific gene-perturbation conditions by minimizing the difference between predicted and ground-truth mean expression shifts."
            ],
            "methods": [
              {
                "method_id": "m1",
                "name": "AttentionPert",
                "protocol_description": "AttentionPert takes perturbation indicators as input into two modules: PertWeight and PertLocal encoders. Each outputs an encoding matrix (RK×D). The sum is fed into a gene-specific linear decoder to predict the expression shift. The prediction is added to a random control sample. Loss function combines auto-focus and direction-aware loss (GEARS). Hyperparameters: embedding size De=200 (Gene2Vec), SGConv hops t=1, hidden size D=64, attention heads H=2, head dimension dq=dk=dv=64, GO graph edge weight multiplier α=0.75, NA-bias β=0.05, trained for 20 epochs, batch size 128, Adam optimizer with learning rate 1e-3."
              },
              {
                "method_id": "m2",
                "name": "PertWeight encoder",
                "protocol_description": "Embeds genes into weight embedding Ew and pert embedding Ep. Applies four SGConv GNN encoders on the GO graph to produce Q, K, V, P. V is masked by perturbation indicators. Multi-head attention computes weighted global effects, combined with P via addition and feed-forward layers to produce HPW."
              },
              {
                "method_id": "m3",
                "name": "PertLocal encoder",
                "protocol_description": "Applies SGConv on augmented GO graph to produce B. Masks B by perturbation indicators. Optionally includes NA-bias module to predict nonadditive effects. Outputs HPL."
              },
              {
                "method_id": "m4",
                "name": "Gene-specific linear decoder",
                "protocol_description": "Takes sum of HPW and HPL; for each gene k, a linear layer maps the encoding to scalar perturbation effect (per-gene weights wk and bias bk). Abandons cross-gene layer used in GEARS."
              },
              {
                "method_id": "m5",
                "name": "Pre-trained Gene2Vec initialization",
                "protocol_description": "All gene embeddings (Ew, Ep, EB) initialized with 200D Gene2Vec vectors derived from co-expression across 984 GEO datasets; can be fine-tuned during training."
              },
              {
                "method_id": "m6",
                "name": "Gene Ontology graph construction",
                "protocol_description": "GO graph J built with edge weights equal to fraction of shared Gene Ontology terms between two genes, following GEARS (Roohani et al. 2023). Augmented GO graph includes additional NA-bias edges with weight β."
              }
            ],
